@participant8 In your case it seems to be something else; please double-check that bgp control plane is enabled and you have restarted the cilium agents since enabling it. If the issue persists, please open a new issue with a sysdump.

This issue has been identified as a problem with 2 (and more) router instances per node, I was able to reproduce it for both BGPv1 and BGPv2 and will work on a fix.

In the meantime, the workaround is to use only single BGP instance per node. In BGPv2 it is possible to configure per-address-family and per-peer specific advertisements, so unless multiple local ASNs are required for some reason, this should allow for enough flexibility even for more complex setups.
